__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Evidence artefacts. Tools write reports, JSON dumps and captures wherever the
# operator points them, which is often the working directory during
# development. None of it belongs in the repository.
#
# --dump takes an arbitrary path, so there is no filename pattern that catches
# every dump; the rule stays broad rather than let a captured topology reach a
# commit. Config that does belong in the tree is named below — add to that list
# rather than narrowing the rule, or the next dump lands in a diff.
# pcap* not pcap: tcpdump's -C rotation appends a number, so ringcap writes
# cap.pcap0, cap.pcap1 … and pads with leading zeros past nine files. The
# trailing wildcard also covers pcapng.
*.pcap*
*.log
*.json
!.mcp.json
!tests/**/*.json
.DS_Store
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
